# SwiftUI Pro (project skill)

When writing or reviewing SwiftUI in EasyStream, read `.cursor/skills/swiftui-pro/SKILL.md` and load only the reference files relevant to the task:

| Area | Reference |
|------|-----------|
| Views, layout, animation | `references/views.md` |
| Performance, identity | `references/performance.md` |
| State / data flow | `references/data.md` |
| Deprecated API | `references/api.md` |
| Accessibility | `references/accessibility.md` |

## EasyStream-specific priorities

1. **Video tiles & PROG monitor** — stable view identity; one `NSViewRepresentable` per slot; no `GeometryReader` for aspect ratio; use custom `Layout` (`BroadcastAspectRatioLayout`, `BroadcastFixedSizeLayout`).
2. **Director switcher** — one `View` struct per file under `EasyStream/Features/Director/`; no `@ViewBuilder` computed properties in `body`; disable implicit layout animation on source changes (`.animation(nil, value:)`).
3. **Theme** — prefer `BroadcastTheme.primaryText` / `subtleText` and `foregroundStyle()` over `.primary` / `.secondary` in studio windows.
4. **Buttons** — always provide accessibility labels for icon-only or video tiles.

